{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIyL01hbWFzJTIwQm95JTIwJTI4MjAyMiUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Mamas Boy","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/drebHXMLSZJ0RwUxc5VpwZEp9X2.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/v0eep6siVRyhVeJknbOXpqZna1H.jpg","description":"Traveling back to the places where he grew up, Dustin Lance Black explores his childhood roots, gay identity and close relationship with his mother, who overcame childhood polio, abusive marriages and Mormon dogma, while becoming Black’s emotional rock and, ultimately, the inspiration for his activism. With a wealth of personal photographs and candid memories from Black’s family, colleagues, and friends, this documentary embraces the personal to tell a universally hopeful tale of resilience and reconciliation through the power of love and shared stories.\n\nReleased 18 Oct 2022 · United States of America · Language: English · 102 min\nStudio: LD Entertainment, Amblin Television, Playtone\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2022","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"3.0","imdb_id":"tt14871116","moviedb_id":1024528,"tmdbId":1024528,"runtime":"102 min","cast":["Dustin Lance Black","Tom Daley","Paris Barclay","Troy Williams"],"director":["Laurent Bouzereau"],"released":"2022-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"Our differences will not divide us","country":"United States of America","language":"English","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Laurent Bouzereau","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/1gVpS5EGGwXXry6xSXo8xfkDlBu.jpg"},{"name":"Dustin Lance Black","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/fFTO10hKeZ2286i72a7GFPaM2Q5.jpg"},{"name":"Tom Daley","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/aVqRe756kcAF93VtYidNheCevLg.jpg"},{"name":"Paris Barclay","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/ovu2mHjElDUfVbXyWoXsowbumDd.jpg"},{"nam